  "question": {
    "text": "The white precipitate $(Y)$, obtained on passing colourless and odourless gas $(X)$ through an ammoniacal solution of $\\mathrm{NaCl}$, loses about $37 \\%$ of its weight on heating and a white residue $(\\mathrm{Z})$ of basic nature is left. Identify $(\\mathrm{X}),(\\mathrm{Y})$ and $(\\mathrm{Z})$ from following sets.",
